1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,460
Business Case 09 begins when an authorized human decision selects the
offer path.

2
00:00:05,460 --> 00:00:10,920
A version-bound candidate response reserves an opening and creates an
eligible pre-hire handoff.

3
00:00:10,920 --> 00:00:13,020
The governed record is OFF-DEMO-001.

4
00:00:13,020 --> 00:00:18,061
The accountable actors are Recruiter, Hiring Manager, Offer Approver,
Candidate, People Operations.

5
00:00:18,061 --> 00:00:24,361
This demonstration uses synthetic browser-memory data and creates no
database, provider, message or external-system effect.

6
00:00:24,361 --> 00:00:29,443
The action-level data-flow diagram defines 4 processes before product
navigation.

7
00:00:29,443 --> 00:00:38,590
Every process identifies the actor, screen, action, input, output,
business object, event, governed store, rule, denial and recovery.

8
00:00:38,590 --> 00:00:43,672
The highlighted path keeps each business grain and version distinct.

9
00:00:43,672 --> 00:00:46,095
Process 1, Recruiter: Compose versioned offer.

10
00:00:46,095 --> 00:00:51,747
The action build terms and contingencies produces validated offer draft
in the Offer ledger.

11
00:00:51,747 --> 00:00:54,573
Process 2, Offer Approver: Approve exact version.

12
00:00:54,573 --> 00:00:59,821
The action approve, return or deny produces approval timeline in the
Approval ledger.

13
00:00:59,821 --> 00:01:02,647
Process 3, Candidate: Respond to exact version.

14
00:01:02,647 --> 00:01:08,299
The action accept, decline or ask question produces version-bound
response in the Offer ledger.

15
00:01:08,299 --> 00:01:11,529
Process 4, People Operations: Reserve and hand off.

16
00:01:11,529 --> 00:01:17,988
The action validate contingencies and create prehire produces opening
reservation and prehire in the Handoff ledger.

17
00:01:17,988 --> 00:01:20,861
The actual product route is /hr/decisions/APP-DEMO-001.

18
00:01:20,861 --> 00:01:28,524
It presents offer composer, version comparison and contingency board in
the surrounding recruitment or onboarding workspace.

19
00:01:28,524 --> 00:01:40,496
The screen remains a wireframe, but its identifiers, current state,
navigation, data relationships and action boundaries match the business
contract used by the connected workbench.

20
00:01:40,496 --> 00:01:43,472
The seeded workbench follows record OFF-DEMO-001.

21
00:01:43,472 --> 00:02:00,835
Its governed fields are Base salary, $182,000 USD; Equity, 8,500 RSUs ,
returned scenario 9,200; Start date, November 16, 2026; Offer version,
v4 , 2 approvers; Opening, OPN-001 , reservable; Contingencies,
Background review , pending.

22
00:02:00,835 --> 00:02:10,261
Field classifications remain visible so the presenter can distinguish
public, internal, confidential and restricted projections for the active
persona.

23
00:02:10,261 --> 00:02:16,323
With Recruiter selected, we perform approve and release offer v4.

24
00:02:16,323 --> 00:02:23,598
The guard requires decision, pay policy, approvals, opening and
contingencies are current.

25
00:02:23,598 --> 00:02:38,755
The state changes from Draft v4 to Released v4, records OfferReleased,
writes to the Offer ledger, and creates the handoff: Candidate receives
exact-version response task.

26
00:02:38,755 --> 00:02:42,913
We now exercise the controlled exception: Simulate compensation return.

27
00:02:42,913 --> 00:02:47,070
The prepared failure is Compensation approver returns equity term.

28
00:02:47,070 --> 00:02:56,771
Unsupported downstream work stops, successful prior evidence remains
intact, and the state-change receipt assigns explicit recovery without
hiding the failed attempt.

29
00:02:56,771 --> 00:03:00,064
The owned recovery is Revise and reapprove v5.

30
00:03:00,064 --> 00:03:04,179
It reuses the governed business context without duplicating completed
effects.

31
00:03:04,179 --> 00:03:09,529
The new receipt preserves previous state, current state, actor, event
and correlation key.

32
00:03:09,529 --> 00:03:18,995
The control center and handoff inbox then expose the same recovery
through offer approval time, version churn and acceptance and
minimum-context next-actor work.

33
00:03:18,995 --> 00:03:21,533
Business Case 09 is complete.

34
00:03:21,533 --> 00:03:36,250
We demonstrated the level-two process contract, the actual product
route, governed field projections, the primary state transition, a
controlled exception, targeted recovery, causal dashboard evidence and
the next-actor handoff.

35
00:03:36,250 --> 00:03:42,848
A version-bound candidate response reserves an opening and creates an
eligible pre-hire handoff.

36
00:03:42,848 --> 00:03:48,430
Production identity, persistence, integrations and external delivery
remain separate implementation gates.
